## Code Example
```c
typedef struct Block {
    struct Block* next;
    uintptr_t tag;
    unsigned char data[128];
} Block;

static _Atomic(Block*) g_free_list = NULL;

static Block* fetch_chunk(void) {
    Block* chunk = aligned_alloc(64, 256 * sizeof(Block));
    for (int i = 0; i < 255; i++) {
        chunk[i].next = &chunk[i + 1];
        chunk[i].tag = 0;
    }
    chunk[255].next = NULL;
    chunk[255].tag = 0;
    return chunk;
}

static Block* alloc_block(void) {
    Block* b = local_cache;  // thread-local
    do {
        if (b) return b;
    } while ((b = atomic_load_explicit(&g_free_list, memory_order_acquire)) 
             && !atomic_compare_exchange_weak(&g_free_list, &b, b->next));
    return b ? b : fetch_chunk();
}
```

## Microbenchmark Plan
1. **Baseline**: Measure allocation latency with warm local cache
2. **Contention test**: Scale threads from 8 to 32, measure global pool miss rate
3. **NUMA sensitivity**: Pin threads to cores on different sockets, measure cross-socket access overhead
4. **Metrics**: Track local-cache hits, global-pool fetches, CAS retry rate, and allocation/free latency percentiles

## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of crash‑consistency in non‑volatile memory, proper cache‑line flush semantics, and cross‑socket ordering. It probes how to design durable queues and recoveries with minimal latency impact.

## Key Concepts
- PMEM durability and flush/fence ordering (clwb/clflushopt, sfence)
- Release/acquire memory ordering and per‑slot sequencing
- Crash recovery and replay correctness in a bounded buffer

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo enqueue (high level, non‑blocking semantics)
function enqueue(slot, payload){
  slot.payload = payload; // write payload
  slot.len = payload.length;
  slot.seq = slot.seq + 1; // release semantics
  clwb(&slot.payload); clwb(&slot.len); clwb(&slot.seq);
  sfence();
}
```

```javascript
// Pseudo dequeue
function dequeue(){
  if (ring.head.seq == ring.tail.seq) return null; // empty
  let s = ring.head; let payload = s.payload;
  // advance head after acquire read
  ring.head = next(s);
  s.done = true; clwb(&s.done); sfence();
  return payload;
}
```
